"""
reagent_hashmap.py

Maps raw reagent strings (from reagents_standard_v1.csv) to canonical forms.
Unmapped reagents (no matching canonical found) have value None.

Canonical categories:
  Solvents:          tetrahydrofuran, dichloromethane, dimethyl sulfoxide, ...
  Acids/Bases:       hydrochloric acid, potassium carbonate, LDA, nBuLi, ...
  Phosphine ligands: BINAP, DPPF, XPhos, SPhos, RuPhos, PPh3, ...
  Nitrogen ligands:  2,2'-bipyridine, 1,10-phenanthroline, DABCO, salen, ...
  NHC ligands:       IPr, IMes, SIPr, SIMes, NHC ligand (generic)
  Pd catalysts:      palladium acetate, Pd(dppf)Cl2, Pd(PPh3)4, Pd-PEPPSI, ...
  Other metals:      Ni/Ru/Rh/Ir/Cu specific complexes + generic fallbacks
  Gas:               carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, hydrogen gas, ...
  Oxidants:          mCPBA, NBS, Dess-Martin periodinane, TEMPO, ...
  Reductants:        NaBH4, LiAlH4, DIBAL, SmI2, ...
  Coupling reagents: EDCI, HATU, DCC, CDI, T3P, ...

Fixes vs v1:
  - \bv\b removed from vanadium (was matching w/v, v/v, voltages)
  - \bco\b disambiguated: CO gas -> carbon monoxide, Co( -> cobalt catalyst
  - \bipr\b restricted to NHC/metal context (was matching isopropyl)
  - \bether\b removed (was matching aryl ethers, substrate ethers)
  - \bedc\b excluded co-solvent context (DCE misidentified as EDCI)
  - \bag\b excludes Ag/AgCl reference electrode entries
  - nitrogen atmosphere excludes liquid N2, diazonium, O2/N2 mixtures
"""


